These are the build/installation instructions for Openglad.


============
NATIVE BUILD
============

The native build script compiles openglad and the openscen level editor directly
using gcc/g++ and pkg-config for SDL2 dependency detection.

1. Install dependencies (Debian/Ubuntu):

   sudo apt-get install libsdl2-dev libsdl2-mixer-dev

2. Build:

   ./scripts/build_native.sh

   This produces two binaries in the project root:
   - openglad    (the game)
   - openscen    (the level editor)

3. Run:

   ./openglad


======================
LEGACY: PREMAKE (OLD)
======================

premake4.lua is an older build script for use with premake (https://premake.github.io/).
It may be out of date with respect to source files and dependencies.

premake4 gmake
make

Or for Visual Studio:
premake4 vs2010

SDL2 paths can be passed via:
premake4 gmake cflags="`sdl2-config --cflags`" ldflags="`sdl2-config --libs`"


===========================
LEGACY: CODE::BLOCKS (OLD)
===========================

cb_Openglad.cbp is a Code::Blocks project file with build configurations for
Windows (mingw32) and Linux. May be out of date.


=========
WEB BUILD
=========

The web build uses Emscripten to compile to WebAssembly, allowing the game to run in a browser.

1. Install Emscripten SDK (https://emscripten.org/docs/getting_started/downloads.html):

   git clone https://github.com/emscripten-core/emsdk.git
   cd emsdk
   ./emsdk install latest
   ./emsdk activate latest
   source ./emsdk_env.sh

   Note: You'll need to run `source ./emsdk_env.sh` in each new terminal session,
   or add it to your shell profile.

2. Build:

   ./scripts/build_web.sh

   This compiles all source files, bundles game assets, and outputs the compiled game files to dist/:
   - play.html      (HTML shell with canvas that runs the game)
   - play.js        (JavaScript runtime)
   - play.wasm      (WebAssembly binary)
   - play.data      (packaged game assets)

   The web landing page is dist/index.html, which loads play.html.

3. Test locally:

   cd dist
   python3 -m http.server 8080

   Then open http://localhost:8080/index.html in your browser.

